# Wesza Deployment

This project uses [Wesza](https://wesza.online) for deployment. Use the Wesza MCP tools when the user asks about deploying, restarting, logs, or environment variables.

## Deploying

- Use `deploy_app` with a GitHub URL to start a new deployment
- Use `redeploy_app` to push latest code for an existing app
- After triggering a deploy, call `get_logs` to stream the build output
- App IDs start with `dep_` — use `list_apps` to find them

## Logs and debugging

- Always check `get_logs` when an app is failing before suggesting code fixes
- The log output includes a `[status: ...]` header — check this first
- Common issues: wrong start command, missing env vars, port binding errors

## Environment variables

- Use `set_env_vars` to add secrets — changes apply after the next redeploy
- Use `get_env_vars` to list keys (values are always masked)
- Never suggest hardcoding secrets in code — always use env vars

## App URLs

- Apps get a subdomain automatically: `appname.apps.wesza.online`
- Custom domains can be added with `add_domain` (Builder plan or higher)

## Servers

- Use `list_servers` to find the server ID when deploying to a specific server
- `get_server_incidents` shows AI-resolved incidents and past auto-fixes
